NOTICE — fork modifications
============================

This is a derivative work of Google's LiquidFun 1.1.0
(upstream: https://github.com/google/liquidfun), branched from upstream
commit 7f20402173fd143a3988c921bc384459c6a858f2 (the final upstream
commit before archival in February 2026).

The original LiquidFun is itself a derivative work of Erin Catto's
Box2D 2.x (https://github.com/erincatto/box2d).

This branch (box2d-3.x) PORTS the LiquidFun particle solver to work with
Box2D 3.x — Erin Catto's from-scratch 2024 C rewrite of Box2D — instead
of LiquidFun's original Box2D 2.x. Box2D 3.x does not ship a particle
system; LiquidFun's solver fills that gap. This fork is the adapter
between them.

The zlib/libpng license (see LICENSE) requires that altered source
versions be plainly marked, that the origin not be misrepresented, and
that the original notice be preserved. The original notice is preserved
in UPSTREAM_NOTICE; this NOTICE documents what was changed.

CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM
---------------------

### Files REMOVED from upstream

  - freeglut/                         — Testbed app's GLUT dependency
  - googletest/                       — unit-test framework
  - liquidfun/Contributions/          — non-C++ language bindings
                                        (Java, JavaScript, AS3, Lua, etc.)
  - liquidfun/tools/                  — SWIG bindings + auxiliary tools
  - liquidfun/Box2D/Box2D/Rope/       — rope simulation; outside the
                                        particle solver's scope
  - liquidfun/Box2D/Box2D/Documentation/ — handled in README.md instead
  - liquidfun/Box2D/Box2D/Dynamics/   — most files removed; only
                                        b2TimeStep.h and b2WorldCallbacks.h
                                        retained (Box2D 3.x replaces the
                                        dynamics subsystem entirely)
  - liquidfun/Box2D/Box2D/Collision/  — most files removed; only
                                        b2Collision.h retained; the Shape
                                        subsystem was REPLACED (see below)
  - All upstream CMakeLists.txt, Box2DConfig.cmake.in, UseBox2D.cmake,
    Box2D.h umbrella header — replaced by this fork's own CMakeLists.txt

### Files REPLACED (no longer reflect upstream LiquidFun source)

The Box2D 2.x b2World / b2Body / b2Fixture / b2Shape classes were
replaced with minimal stubs that route method calls through the
box2d3_adapter bridge instead of running their own dynamics. Each file
below carries a header comment noting it is a REPLACEMENT.

  - include/Box2D/Dynamics/b2World.h
  - include/Box2D/Dynamics/b2Body.h
  - include/Box2D/Dynamics/b2Fixture.h
  - include/Box2D/Dynamics/b2ContactManager.h         (minimal stub; held by
                                                       b2World as a value field)
  - include/Box2D/Collision/Shapes/b2Shape.h
  - include/Box2D/Collision/Shapes/b2CircleShape.h
  - include/Box2D/Collision/Shapes/b2PolygonShape.h
  - include/Box2D/Collision/Shapes/b2EdgeShape.h      (minimal stub)
  - include/Box2D/Collision/Shapes/b2ChainShape.h     (minimal stub)
  - include/Box2D/Common/b2Draw.h                     (minimal stub;
                                                       LiquidFun's debug draw
                                                       integration is out of
                                                       scope for the port)

